{"name":"Ottawa Falls","hex":"#00a78d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"falls","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A waterfall."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of fall"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/falls"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ottawa","blocks":[{"text":"Ottawa is the capital city of Canada. It is located in the southeastern portion of the province of Ontario, at the confluence of the Ottawa River and the Rideau River. Ottawa borders Gatineau, Quebec, and forms the core of the Ottawa–Gatineau census metropolitan area (CMA) and the National Capital Region (NCR). As of 2021, Ottawa had a city population of 1,017,449 and a metropolitan population of 1,488,307, making it the fourth-largest city and fourth-largest metropolitan area in Canada."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Parliament-Ottawa.jpg/330px-Parliament-Ottawa.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ottawa","wikidata":"Q1930"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Rideau_Canal_at_downtown_Ottawa.JPG/500px-Rideau_Canal_at_downtown_Ottawa.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Rideau_Canal_at_downtown_Ottawa.JPG/1280px-Rideau_Canal_at_downtown_Ottawa.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Rideau_Canal_at_downtown_Ottawa.JPG/500px-Rideau_Canal_at_downtown_Ottawa.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARideau_Canal_at_downtown_Ottawa.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/10_Rideau_Hall_P1350151.jpg/500px-10_Rideau_Hall_P1350151.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content